Object.assign(saturniaMediaRecord, {"type": "Archmage · Keeper of the Arcane Secrets", "dek": "A legendary Zuk’Teuc scholar, the sage in Scribonia’s spellbook, and a demigod bound to guard arcane secrets.", "tags": ["Saturnia", "Thri-kreen", "Zuk’Teuc", "Archmage", "Manifest Mind", "Arcane secrets", "Demigod"], "facts": {"People": "Thri-kreen · Zuk’Teuc", "Known office": "Keeper of the Arcane Secrets", "Divine status": "Demigod", "Ascension": "Date and mechanism unresolved"}, "sources": ["Saturnia_Ultimate_Fenumion_Codex_Entry.md · revealed RP and public-knowledge sections, received 7 October 2026", "User-supplied arrival video and goddess portrait · 7 October 2026"], "body": "<p>Saturnia is a legendary Thri-kreen archmage of the Zuk’Teuc, the ancestral people also associated with Scribonia. Her books outlasted her disappearance generations ago. To Scribonia she became a model of scholarship: a great sage whose image accompanied his own pursuit of arcane knowledge. Later testimony identifies her as a demigod and Keeper of the Arcane Secrets, although the circumstances of her ascension remain unknown.</p>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-scholar\">The scholar beyond her maps</h2><p>A Legend Lore vision recovered on 21 September 2026 shows a younger Saturnia arriving in Fenumion. Darkness and void give way to a flash and a gate different from the one modern adventurers know, but serving the same purpose. Saturnia carries books and many maps. None describe the land before her.</p><p>She appears young and inexperienced, confronted by a place her preparations cannot explain. A blond human paladin in shining armor approaches and introduces himself as Ser Kurayami. He welcomes her to the “fractured continent of Fenumion,” says the gods have sent a scholar, and warns that she will need knowledge of the arcane. This is a recovered glimpse of her arrival, not a complete account of her early travels. The ancient scene’s date and the duration of their acquaintance are not established.</p>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-arrival\">Young Saturnia on arrival</h2><figure class=\"arrival-recording\"><video class=\"ambient-video\" data-ambient-video muted loop playsinline disablepictureinpicture disableremoteplayback tabindex=\"-1\" preload=\"metadata\" aria-label=\"Young Saturnia on arrival\"><source src=\"assets/characters/saturnia-arrival.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">Your browser does not support this video. <a href=\"assets/characters/saturnia-arrival.mp4\">Open the arrival video.</a></video><figcaption>Young Saturnia on arrival. Depiction supplied by the world’s creator.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-manifest-mind\">The sage in the spellbook</h2><p>Scribonia’s Manifest Mind takes Saturnia’s form. On 15 June 2024 a small spectral figure emerges from his spellbook, scouting and letting him see and cast through it. A later clarification describes the apparition as a roughly one-foot, ghostlike moth person. These scenes establish the spellbook manifestation; they do not establish that every appearance is the demigod personally intervening.</p><p>Her image also appears in a magical temptation on 27 June 2024. A vision of the great archmage offers Scribonia a seat and all the magical secrets he seeks while the Zuk’Teuc bow. The offer uses Saturnia’s appearance. It is not confirmed dialogue from the real Saturnia, and cannot be treated as proof of her intentions.</p><p>The manifestation is often joyful. On 11 July 2024 she dances through a library on phantom winds. On 4 November Scribonia summons a figure to scale to help him mirror a dance. By 19 August 2025 the manifestation stands at full height, shining like the North Star. Her starry dress reverses the colors of Scribonia’s clothing as their dance combines ballroom movement with Thri-kreen wings, antennae and abdominal flourishes. The scenes show how much warmth and companionship her image holds for him.</p>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-sacrifice\">What knowledge costs</h2><p>On 5 August 2024, when Moirah asks for a meaningful sacrifice, Scribonia summons a tiny Saturnia and holds the sad, sagelike figure in his hands. He apologizes to the Great Sage and says he wishes he could have met her. Closing and raising his spellbook, he offers his knowledge; blue energy accompanies Saturnia’s disappearance into the book.</p><p>The sacrifice expresses what scholarship means to him. It does not establish the death or destruction of Saturnia herself. Later manifestations remain part of the recovered record.</p>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-keeper\">Keeper of the Arcane Secrets</h2><p>On 30 May 2026 Eugene asks Vesperax who Saturnia is. Vesperax calls her the Keeper of the Arcane Secrets, an ancient vassal of the First God, bound to protect the realm’s arcana. This testimony gives her divine role a sharper meaning: the pursuit of knowledge has become a duty to guard it.</p><p>The record confirms demigodhood but leaves the transition unexplained. It does not identify the First God, date Saturnia’s ascension, or settle whether her binding was freely chosen. Her current location and the extent of direct intervention are likewise unresolved. The supplied portrait depicts Saturnia the goddess; it is kept distinct from the younger arrival recording.</p>\n<h2 id=\"saturnia-scribonia\">Scribonia’s questions</h2><p>By September 2026 Scribonia is investigating the relationship between the ancestral archmage and the divine figure. His account reports that Saturnia has taken an interest in his continued existence and used the words “my child.” That familial language prompts questions about a possible divine mother; it does not establish literal biological parenthood.</p><p>On 19 September he casts Legend Lore from an armchair in his pocket realm. The arrival scene follows on 21 September. Seeing Saturnia enter the unknown with her books and maps, he recognizes something of his own path in hers and considers seeking the Guardians for further answers. What happened between that arrival and her later office remains an open historical question.</p><h2 id=\"saturnia-history-events\">Saturnia in the timeline</h2><p>Dates identify recovered modern scenes. The ancient arrival is dated by its September 2026 revelation, not by an invented ancient calendar date.</p><ol class=\"location-timeline-list\"><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Scribonia’s spellbook manifests Saturnia\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">15 Jun 2024</span><strong>Scribonia’s spellbook manifests Saturnia</strong><span>A small spectral Saturnia emerges from Scribonia’s spellbook to scout and serve as a point through which he can see and cast.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"A temptation wears Saturnia’s face\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">27 Jun 2024</span><strong>A temptation wears Saturnia’s face</strong><span>A magical vision uses Saturnia’s appearance to offer Scribonia all the secrets he seeks. The promise is not confirmed speech from the real Saturnia.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Saturnia’s manifestation dances through a library\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">11 Jul 2024</span><strong>Saturnia’s manifestation dances through a library</strong><span>The spellbook manifestation dances on phantom winds, showing the joyful presence Saturnia’s image holds for Scribonia.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Scribonia offers his knowledge to Moirah\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">5 Aug 2024</span><strong>Scribonia offers his knowledge to Moirah</strong><span>Scribonia apologizes to the tiny Saturnia manifestation and offers his knowledge. Blue energy accompanies its return to the spellbook; the scene does not establish Saturnia’s death.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Saturnia’s manifestation helps Scribonia mirror a dance\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">4 Nov 2024</span><strong>Saturnia’s manifestation helps Scribonia mirror a dance</strong><span>Scribonia summons a to-scale Saturnia to help him mirror a dance.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Scribonia dances with a star-bright Saturnia\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">19 Aug 2025</span><strong>Scribonia dances with a star-bright Saturnia</strong><span>A full-height Saturnia manifestation shines like the North Star as their dance combines ballroom steps and Thri-kreen flourishes.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Vesperax names Saturnia’s arcane duty\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">30 May 2026</span><strong>Vesperax names Saturnia’s arcane duty</strong><span>Vesperax identifies Saturnia as Keeper of the Arcane Secrets and ancient vassal of the First God, bound to guard the realm’s arcana.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Scribonia investigates Saturnia through Legend Lore\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">19 Sep 2026</span><strong>Scribonia investigates Saturnia through Legend Lore</strong><span>Scribonia casts Legend Lore while asking how Saturnia is connected to him. Familial language raises a question of divine motherhood without settling biological parenthood.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li><li><button type=\"button\" class=\"location-timeline-event\" data-timeline-title=\"Legend Lore reveals Saturnia’s arrival\"><span class=\"location-timeline-date\">21 Sep 2026</span><strong>Legend Lore reveals Saturnia’s arrival</strong><span>A vision shows young Saturnia carrying books and maps into Fenumion, where Ser Kurayami welcomes her to the fractured continent. This dates the revelation, not the ancient arrival.</span><small>Open timeline record →</small></button></li></ol>"});
