articles.find(record => record.id === "memorable-quotes").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "memorable-quotes").body.replace('<h2 id="why-these-lines-remain">', "<h2 id=\"babel-quotes-3473\">Babel’s survivors · Nights, stories and promises</h2><button type=\"button\" class=\"quote-card\" data-article=\"quille\"><blockquote>“Each night is a success. Trust us, we count our sleeps.”</blockquote><cite>Quille</cite></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"quote-card\" data-article=\"omari\"><blockquote>“We got stories. Stories are what keep people going. Keep the old walking and the young from growing weary.”</blockquote><cite>Omari</cite></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"quote-card\" data-article=\"gartina\"><blockquote>“Sing the names of those you know but see no longer. Resist the erasure of your past with all you have.”</blockquote><cite>Gartina</cite></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"quote-card\" data-article=\"arjahn\"><blockquote>“We all break at some point. What matters is that we put ourselves back together. We don’t have to be the same as we were before. We don’t even have to be similar. We just have to live on.”</blockquote><cite>Arjahn</cite></button><h2 id=\"babel-quotes-126\">Dale and Saray · A lesson in trust</h2><button type=\"button\" class=\"quote-card\" data-article=\"saray\"><blockquote>“You got this Dale! I know you don&#x27;t believe you are too much. But believe when I tell you...you are a decisive piece in this war. We need you.”</blockquote><cite>Saray</cite></button>" + '<h2 id="why-these-lines-remain">');
articles.find(record => record.id === "akarian").body += '<h2 id="akarian-dale-saray">A lesson in defended weaknesses</h2><p>In the training account posted on 12 October 2024 (UTC), Akarian tests Dale and Saray against enemies that exploit magical control, reliance on blindsight and their concern for one another. The exercise ends in defeat. He heals the pair and pulls them out, making the encounter a lesson to survive and learn from rather than a battlefield death.</p>';
const babelVanguardRecord = articles.find(record => record.id === "vanguard");
babelVanguardRecord.body = babelVanguardRecord.body.replace("first and only direct Vanguard reference", "early direct Vanguard reference");
babelVanguardRecord.body += '<h2 id="vanguard-primary-context">The first wave and the next</h2><p>In the primary Babel account posted on 6 May 2026 (UTC), Mya describes the scattered and battered first wave and says Nuru is preparing a more focused second Vanguard. She asks the veterans either to help pass power and knowledge onward or to reunite and prove the gods wrong. At the later survivors’ gathering, Gartina also calls her companions Vanguard. These statements broaden the term’s surviving use; they do not supply a complete roster, ranks, charter or chain of command.</p>';
for (const title of babelReconnaissanceTitles) {const event = archiveIndex.timeline.find(record => record.title === title); if (event) event.era = "2026 · Consequences";}

// Selected Common Man primary scenes: hospitality, memorial and recovery.
// Dates refer to UTC posts unless an in-world date is independently established.
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("<h2 id=\"december-15\">", "<h2 id=\"hospitality-and-work\">Hospitality, work and a place to begin</h2><p>In the account posted on 16 March 2024, Nienna helps Gartina approach Herb about kitchen work. Gartina offers early-morning baking; Herb offers ingredients and modest pay, conditional on the goods selling, and Gartina accepts. This is one of the tavern’s practical connections between a newcomer’s skills and the town’s daily needs.</p><p>On 6 August, Herb explains that a stipend provides newcomers with a bunk and food while they get oriented. Later that month he credits paying Pristinia customers and a subsidy from <a href=\"#melian-starguard\">Melian</a> with keeping the cookfires lit and the liquor stocked. His beer, Tina’s Tincture, also remembers Gartina and her friends drying the fields so grain could be planted. Hospitality depends on work and reciprocal help, rather than an inexhaustible larder.</p><h2 id=\"december-15\">");
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("<h2 id=\"memory-space\">Memorial and return</h2>", "<h2 id=\"memory-space\">Memorial and return</h2><p>The gathering posted on 25 May 2024 makes remembrance an organized act. <a href=\"#wren\">Wren</a> prepares food and drink and speaks for the fallen; Tricks plays softly, Dale contributes music, and Alyhotep gives a benediction. After the gathering, Wren helps clear the tankards but leaves the memorial in place. Private arguments run alongside the service, but the lasting civic act is the community making room for its dead.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("<p>Zombie pirates eventually burn the Common Man. The exact date, circumstances, people present, and casualties remain unresolved; by July 29, 2026, the destruction is established past history and revenge hunts continue. The loss matters because the target was not a generic tavern. It was where people worked, ate, danced, worried, remembered, and learned how to belong.</p>", "<p>The tavern is already in ruins in posts dated <strong>28 June 2026 (UTC)</strong>. This narrows the latest known limit for the fire; it does not establish the day of the attack. The loss destroys a workplace, a meeting room and a refuge accumulated through years of ordinary life.</p><p>In the following day’s cleanup, Nala Thilxed recalls an undead pirate crew whose captain wore a red-bead necklace. They had been asked to leave; she describes a confrontation with Rose, a fight inside and the captain escaping to fight outside. She says their group got out before the roof collapsed. Selwyn, who says he arrived near the end, also describes an escaped captain and later attributes the fire to a Fireball. These are survivors’ accounts with different vantage points, not a complete battle record. The full casualty count and the captain’s ultimate fate remain unresolved.</p><h3 id=\"common-man-cleanup\">Herb and the people who returned</h3><p>Herb is alive and clearing charred wood in the account posted on 29 June. He refuses to blame the adventurers, thanking them for doing what they could. Camilla Blackwood surveys the foundations and goes to check materials; Lady Severina brings ropes and water, with Øblivion available for hauling. Nala, Selwyn, Saelihn, Ibere, Karnak and Jangir appear among those helping. Karnak supplies wood and stone. These actions establish shared recovery work without assigning the entire rebuilding to one person.</p><p>Moving beams uncovers the charred but intact basement trapdoor. Herb opens it and finds the food and drinks safe. A few tables and stools can also be cleaned and repainted. He brings refreshments to the workers, insisting that they rest. The tavern’s service continues among the ruins before its replacement is finished.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("<p>By July 29, Pilgrim’s Hearth stands on the Common Man’s foundations as “a symbol of growth and change.” By September it is again an active social room for tea, news, and ordinary conversation. The Common Man was not restored exactly, and it was not erased.</p>", "<p>Posts dated 5 July describe a mostly finished tavern and its “new bones,” with debris still being cleared. Odo helps sweep despite having little personal history with the old place; Saelihn remembers helping bring cedar back to town. This records visible progress, not a definitive opening date. By 29 July, <a href=\"#pilgrims-hearth\">Pilgrim’s Hearth</a> stands on the foundations as “a symbol of growth and change.” By September it is again an active social room for tea, news and ordinary conversation.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("<p>The founder and owner, Herb’s and Skye’s fuller histories, the exact fire, the staff’s fate, the builder of Pilgrim’s Hearth, surviving objects or traditions, and the structure’s physical inheritance remain unknown. The archive preserves the succession without inventing those links.</p>", "<p>The account posted on 14 August 2025 identifies Herb as the owner and barkeeper; his own introduction gives his name as <strong>Herb Shepard</strong>. A legal deed and the original founder remain unrecovered. Herb’s survival and salvaged stores and furniture are now established, but the fate of every staff member, the exact fire date, the replacement’s full building history and whether those furnishings were installed in the Hearth remain open.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").body.replace("Zombie pirates burn the tavern; exact chronology remains open.", "Zombie pirates burn the tavern before the ruins are recorded on 28 June 2026; the exact attack date remains open.");
articles.find(record => record.id === "herb").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "herb").body.replace("<p>Herb helps make <a href=\"#common-man\">the Common Man</a> legible as an institution rather than scenery. Food, wages, tips, exhausted farmers, music, strangers, and regular orders all meet at the bar. The record sometimes calls it “Herb’s tavern,” but legal ownership has not been recovered; the Codex preserves him as a major staff figure without inventing a title.</p>", "<p>Herb helps make <a href=\"#common-man\">the Common Man</a> legible as an institution rather than scenery. The narration posted on 14 August 2025 explicitly calls him its <strong>owner and barkeeper</strong>. Later in that exchange he introduces himself as <strong>Herb Shepard</strong>; the record also contains the spellings Sheperd and Shepherd. The direct introduction supplies the spelling used here. A legal deed and founding history remain unrecovered.</p><h2 id=\"herb-hospitality\">Making arrival possible</h2><p>Herb offers Gartina ingredients and modest pay for morning baking in the March 2024 account. In August he explains that newcomers receive a bunk and food through a stipend while finding their feet. He credits full-paying locals and Melian’s subsidy with keeping the tavern supplied. His work gives practical form to the welcome adventurers receive.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "herb").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "herb").body.replace("<p>Zombie pirates later burn the Common Man, and <a href=\"#pilgrims-hearth\">Pilgrim’s Hearth</a> rises on the same foundations. Herb survives both a personal death and the destruction of the ordinary place through which the archive first knows him. The source associates him with the successor era without establishing that he founded, owns, or formally manages the new tavern.</p>", "<p>Herb survives the Common Man’s destruction. In the cleanup posted on 29 June 2026, he clears debris, thanks the adventurers and refuses to blame them for the loss. When the basement is opened, he finds its stores intact and serves the helpers wine, food, juice and water. His idea of the tavern survives its walls: a place where people can forget their worries for a while and treat common folk as equals.</p><p>He also recoils when talk turns to retaliation and war, remembering how much Pristinia lost in its previous conflict. That is a civilian’s fear of renewed suffering, not a formal decision by the town. His eventual position in <a href=\"#pilgrims-hearth\">Pilgrim’s Hearth</a> remains unresolved.</p>");
Object.assign(articles.find(record => record.id === "herb").facts, {Name: "Herb Shepard · also recorded as Sheperd / Shepherd", Role: "Common Man owner and barkeeper", Ownership: "Explicitly identified in the 14 Aug 2025 account; deed unrecovered", "After the fire": "Alive and helping with cleanup in the 29 Jun 2026 account"});
Object.assign(articles.find(record => record.id === "common-man").facts, {Owner: "Herb Shepard · identified in the 14 Aug 2025 account", Fate: "Burned by zombie pirates; ruins recorded 28 Jun 2026 (UTC)", Salvage: "Basement stores and some tables and stools survive"});
articles.find(record => record.id === "wren").body += "<h2 id=\"wren-common-man-memorial\">Keeping the memorial</h2><p>In the Common Man gathering posted on 25 May 2024 (UTC), Wren prepares food and drink and delivers an address honoring the fallen. Tricks and Dale bring music, and Alyhotep gives a benediction. Wren thanks those present, then helps clean up while leaving the memorial itself in place. Her care becomes an act of public memory: the gathering ends, but the dead retain a place in the room.</p>";
articles.find(record => record.id === "gartina").body += "<h2 id=\"gartina-common-man-work\">Baking a place in Pristinia</h2><p>In the tavern account posted on 16 March 2024 (UTC), Nienna encourages Gartina to ask Herb for kitchen work. Gartina offers baked goods before sunrise; Herb offers ingredients and modest pay if they sell, and she accepts. Later, Herb names his beer Tina’s Tincture after her and her friends’ work drying the fields for planting. These are practical contributions remembered in the town’s daily life.</p>";
articles.find(record => record.id === "pilgrims-hearth").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "pilgrims-hearth").body.replace("<p>The builder and owner, its complete floor plan, the fate of the Common Man’s surviving staff, which furnishings or traditions crossed into the new tavern, and how Pristinia formally understands the institution remain unresolved. The supplied moving record establishes the Hearth’s visual identity but does not answer those historical questions.</p>", "<p>The builder and owner, its complete floor plan and which furnishings or staff crossed into the new tavern remain unresolved. The Common Man record does establish Herb alive during cleanup, with intact basement stores and a few salvageable tables and stools. Survival of these objects does not establish their installation in the Hearth. The supplied moving record establishes the Hearth’s visual identity but does not answer those historical questions.</p>");
articles.find(record => record.id === "pilgrims-hearth").body = articles.find(record => record.id === "pilgrims-hearth").body.replace("<h2 id=\"hearth-ordinary-life\">", "<h3 id=\"hearth-new-bones\">The new bones</h3><p>In tavern posts dated 5 July 2026 (UTC), Saelihn sees a mostly finished building and remembers helping bring cedar back to town. Selwyn notices its new bones, while Odo sweeps remaining debris despite having little connection to the old tavern. The scene records recovery already visible in early July; it does not establish the exact opening date or the Hearth’s final name at that moment.</p><h2 id=\"hearth-ordinary-life\">");
for (const id of ["common-man", "herb", "pilgrims-hearth", "wren", "gartina"]) articles.find(record => record.id === id).sources.push("Common Man tavern primary record — selected hospitality, memorial and recovery scenes; dates are UTC posting dates");
for (const record of archiveIndex.npcs) if (record.article === "herb") Object.assign(record, {title: "Herb Shepard", meta: "Common Man owner and barkeeper · Pristinia", summary: "Also recorded as Herb Sheperd / Shepherd. Welcomes newcomers, safeguards supplies and survives to help clear the Common Man’s ruins."});
